        "original_id": "4363c778-b1f9-5d57-93ef-258b1d50c611",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mariana Kovacevic, Asamoah Gyan\n- Roles: traditional healer, professional footballer, striker, national team captain\n- Topics: horse placenta treatment, sports injury healing, 2012 African Cup of Nations\n- Places: Serbia, Gabon, Equatorial Guinea, Accra\n\nFacts:\n- Mariana Kovacevic is a Serbian traditional healer who specializes in using horse placenta treatment to heal athletes.\n- Asamoah Gyan was born on 22 November 1985 in Accra.\n- During the 2012 African Cup of Nations in Gabon and Equatorial Guinea, Mariana Kovacevic used horse placenta treatment on Ghana's Asamoah Gyan after he suffered an injury that was expected to keep him out of football for four weeks.\n- Asamoah Gyan is a Ghanaian professional footballer who plays as a striker for Kayserispor and captains the Ghanaian national team.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
